  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When hydrogen atoms of the amino group of arylamines are replaced by electron donating alkyl groups, the basic character of the resulting amine increases.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0138_6107c2e7fe7f.png\" style=\"width: 380px; height: 177px;\" /></p><p>B.S. order,&nbsp;Phenyl methanamine &gt;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>-Dimethylaniline&nbsp;&gt;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>-Methyl aniline &gt; Benzenamine.</p>"
